V Those of the sock and buskin, artists, court gazetteers—
V Odd fellows all—__odder__ than all their club compeers.
V Some were sub-editors, others reporters,
V And more __illuminati__, joke-importers.
V The club was heterogen’ous
V By strangers seen as
V A refuge for destitute __bons__ __mots__—
V __Dépôt__ for leaden jokes and pewter pots;
V Repertory for gin and __jeux__ __d’esprit__,
V Literary pound for vagrant rapartee;
V Second-hand shop for left-off witticisms;
V Gall’ry for Tomkins and Pitt-icisms;footnote:[A
  play-bill reminiscence, viz. “The scenery by Messrs. Tomkins and Pitt.”—THE AUTHORS OF “BUT, HOWEVER.”] Foundling hospital for every bastard pun;
V In short, a manufactory for all sorts of fun!
V Arouse my muse! such pleasing themes to quit,
V Hear me while I say
V “__Donnez-moi__ __du__ __frenzy,__ __s’il__ __vous__ __plait!__”footnote:[“Donnez-moi,” &amp;c.—The classics of all countries are aptly drawn upon by the universal erudition of our bard. A fine parody this upon the exclamation of Belmontel’s starving author: “La Gloire—donnez-moi do pain!”—FENWICK DE PORQUET.]
V Give me a most tremendous fit
V Of indignation, a wild volcanic ebullition,
V Or deep anathema,
V Fatal as J—d’s bah!
V To hurl excisemen downward to perdition.
V May genial gin no more delight __their__ throttles—
V __Their__ casks grow leaky, bottomless __their__ bottles;
V May smugglers __run__, and they ne’er make a seizure;
V May __they__—I’ll curse them further at my leisure.
V But for our club,
V “Ay, there’s the rub.”
V “We mourn it dead in its father’s halls:”footnote:[“They mourn it dead,” &amp;c.—A pretty, but perhaps too literal allusion to a popular song—J. RODWELL.]—
V The sporting prints are cut down from the walls;
V No stuffing there,
V Not even in a chair;
V The spirits are all __ex__(or)__cised__,
V The coffee-cups capsized,
V The coffee __fine__-d, the snuff all taken,
V The mild Havannahs are by lights forsaken:
V The utter ruin of the club’s achieven—
V Our very chess-boards are ex-__chequered__ even.
