P Looking over some papers the other day in my drawer, with the intention of
  selecting any correspondence that might have passed between myself and the
  duke, I found that his grace had never written to me more than once; but the
  single communication I had received from him was so truly characteristic of the
  man, that I cannot refrain from giving the whole of it. Having heard it re-
